      "message": "In api_kotlin_object.kt, we successfully insert the {{ experimental }} annotation block right before the public external fun. However, if the method starts with get, the generator creates a syntactic Kotlin property (public val {{ name }}) just below it. Because we didn\u0027t add {{ experimental }} to this property block as well, developers will be able to access the property syntax (e.g. obj.experimentalField) without triggering the Kotlin compiler\u0027s opt-in warning. We should make sure to copy the {{ experimental }} macro call to the getter property generation as well. Or is this an intentional design?",
